## 2. Formal mapping

### Standard chemistry

Gibbs free energy:

    ΔG = ΔG° + RT ln Q

where:
- ΔG° is standard free energy (prior),
- R is gas constant,
- T is temperature,
- Q is reaction quotient (current state).

Reaction proceeds spontaneously when ΔG < 0.

### UAF interpretation

- Q is the likelihood of the current state.
- ΔG° is the prior (standard state).
- ΔG is the surprise (distance from equilibrium).
- T is the precision inverse (temperature = noise).

The reaction "wants to" reach equilibrium.
This is gradient descent on energy landscape.

    ḃ_i = -γ_i ∇_{c_i} G({c}) + η_i(t)

where:
- c_i is concentration of species i (belief state),
- G is Gibbs free energy (free energy objective),
- γ_i is kinetic constant (learning rate),
- η_i is thermal noise (exploration).

This is literally the same equation as Active Inference:

    Q(t+1) = Q(t) - α∇F(Q) + noise

but without neurons, without consciousness, without representation.
Pure thermodynamic inference.

