## 4. Connection to L3 (life)

The chemical level produces the ingredients for life:

| L2 Structure | L3 Function |
|---|---|
| Stable molecules | Building blocks (nucleotides, amino acids) |
| Catalysts | Enzymes (protein catalysts) |
| Reaction networks | Metabolism (autocatalytic cycles) |
| Membranes | Cell boundary (autopoiesis) |
| Concentration gradients | Information storage (pre-genetic) |

The transition L2 → L3 occurs when:
1. A reaction network becomes self-sustaining (autocatalysis).
2. The network is enclosed in a membrane (boundary).
3. The network can copy itself (reproduction).

This is the origin of life as a UAF phase transition.

